1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:03,545
[TALIA] <i>So we are continuing this campaign</i>

2
00:00:03,628 --> 00:00:06,589
<i>with our next partner,</i>

3
00:00:06,673 --> 00:00:09,551
<i>Billy Cariño of LoveList.</i>

4
00:00:09,634 --> 00:00:12,971
[BILLY] <i>LoveList stands where it is today</i>

5
00:00:13,054 --> 00:00:15,390
<i>because of my team,</i>

6
00:00:15,473 --> 00:00:17,308
<i>my best friend,</i>

7
00:00:17,392 --> 00:00:19,602
<i>my LoveList family,</i>

8
00:00:20,270 --> 00:00:21,855
<i>and my family.</i>

9
00:00:22,480 --> 00:00:25,316
[BEA] <i>I've done everything I can</i>

10
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:27,736
<i>to give my mother a good life.</i>

11
00:00:27,819 --> 00:00:29,362
[BEA SNIFFLES]

12
00:00:30,155 --> 00:00:31,531
<i>What's happening?</i>

13
00:00:32,198 --> 00:00:33,867
<i>I'm back to square one.</i>

14
00:00:34,993 --> 00:00:35,910
<i>Billy.</i>

15
00:00:36,536 --> 00:00:37,954
<i>Again, I'm sorry.</i>

16
00:00:38,038 --> 00:00:41,583
<i>You know that I love you very much, right?</i>

17
00:00:41,666 --> 00:00:44,836
<i>You're gonna let me see Papa again?</i>

18
00:00:46,546 --> 00:00:47,380
<i>Mm.</i>

19
00:00:47,464 --> 00:00:48,590
<i>Thank you, Billy!</i>

20
00:00:48,673 --> 00:00:50,300
<i>- Thank you.</i>
<i>- Mmm!</i>

21
00:00:50,383 --> 00:00:52,385
<i>Thank you, thank you!</i>

22
00:00:54,345 --> 00:00:55,930
<i>I hope you can forgive me, Precious.</i>

23
00:00:57,474 --> 00:00:59,184
<i>I never meant to hurt you.</i>

24
00:00:59,267 --> 00:01:02,020
<i>I didn't come here</i>
<i>to listen to your explanation.</i>

25
00:01:03,063 --> 00:01:04,606
<i>- But, Pres--</i>
<i>- Listen.</i>

26
00:01:05,231 --> 00:01:09,986
<i>Billy agreed. You can meet with Oliver</i>
<i>after his classes are over.</i>

27
00:01:10,070 --> 00:01:12,113
<i>4:30 to 5:30.</i>

28
00:01:12,739 --> 00:01:14,157
<i>You can meet up at your house.</i>

29
00:01:14,240 --> 00:01:15,950
[JORDAN]
<i>Are you sure about your decision?</i>

30
00:01:17,160 --> 00:01:18,453
<i>My brother's all grown up.</i>

31
00:01:18,536 --> 00:01:20,872
<i>I just want to give him the chance</i>

32
00:01:20,955 --> 00:01:24,000
<i>to meet his father,</i>
<i>even just for a little while.</i>

33
00:01:24,083 --> 00:01:26,544
<i>Then it's up to him</i>
<i>after he gets to know him.</i>

34
00:01:27,253 --> 00:01:28,797
<i>I wish I had your courage.</i>

35
00:01:32,467 --> 00:01:33,426
<i>I'm really sorry.</i>

36
00:01:41,392 --> 00:01:42,644
<i>Let's go.</i>

37
00:01:43,603 --> 00:01:45,730
[WOMAN] <i>What the hell?!</i>
<i>The road is so wide!</i>

38
00:01:45,814 --> 00:01:47,816
- [MARIELA] <i>Just get out of here! Idiot!</i>
- [WOMAN] <i>Dang it!</i>

39
00:01:47,899 --> 00:01:48,942
- [MAN]<i> Come on.</i>
<i>- Idiot!</i>

40
00:01:49,025 --> 00:01:50,068
[MAN] <i>Let's go.</i>

41
00:01:54,823 --> 00:01:55,698
<i>Mariela?</i>

42
00:01:55,782 --> 00:01:57,450
<i>I saw my husband.</i>

43
00:01:58,451 --> 00:02:00,620
<i>The one who hasn't contacted me in years.</i>

44
00:02:00,703 --> 00:02:01,663
[KNOCK AT DOOR]

45
00:02:02,372 --> 00:02:03,498
[PRECIOUS] <i>Mariela?</i>

46
00:02:05,416 --> 00:02:06,668
<i>Bea?</i>

47
00:02:06,751 --> 00:02:09,170
[LYDIA] <i>Sis, let's just leave.</i>

48
00:02:18,721 --> 00:02:22,142
[BILLY] <i>You saw how happy</i>
<i>he was earlier, didn't you?</i>

49
00:02:22,225 --> 00:02:24,269
[NO AUDIBLE DIALOG]

50
00:02:24,352 --> 00:02:28,940
<i>Didn't I tell you</i>
<i>that decision was for Oliver?</i>

51
00:02:29,023 --> 00:02:30,775
<i>But is it the right choice?</i>

52
00:02:31,359 --> 00:02:34,946
<i>Well, we'll never know unless we try.</i>

53
00:02:36,114 --> 00:02:37,824
<i>Okay then. Bye-bye.</i>

54
00:02:37,907 --> 00:02:38,741
<i>Auntie Pres.</i>

55
00:02:38,825 --> 00:02:41,035
<i>Are you all right?</i>

56
00:02:52,130 --> 00:02:58,136
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

57
00:03:15,153 --> 00:03:21,993
["ABELYANA" BY MAKI PLAYING]

58
00:03:35,840 --> 00:03:40,553
["ABELYANA" CONTINUES]

59
00:03:51,064 --> 00:03:52,690
[JORDAN] <i>We've known</i>
<i>each other for so long.</i>

60
00:03:53,942 --> 00:03:55,151
<i>There are good times</i>

61
00:03:55,235 --> 00:03:56,236
<i>and bad.</i>

62
00:03:57,278 --> 00:03:58,696
<i>We've seen it all.</i>

63
00:04:01,991 --> 00:04:08,790
["ABELYANA" CONTINUES]

64
00:04:23,805 --> 00:04:30,353
["ABELYANA" CONTINUES]

65
00:04:43,283 --> 00:04:45,076
[JORDAN] <i>And I can't help</i>

66
00:04:45,159 --> 00:04:47,412
<i>but admire how you rose above it.</i>

67
00:04:49,205 --> 00:04:50,498
<i>I can't help</i>

68
00:04:50,581 --> 00:04:51,833
<i>but fall.</i>

69
00:04:56,254 --> 00:05:01,884
["ABELYANA" CONTINUES]

70
00:05:18,318 --> 00:05:24,657
["ABELYANA" CONTINUES]

71
00:05:40,506 --> 00:05:42,842
[JORDAN]<i> I can't help</i>
<i>but fear losing you.</i>

72
00:05:45,136 --> 00:05:47,055
<i>So let me take this chance to say…</i>

73
00:05:49,932 --> 00:05:51,059
<i>I think I love you.</i>

74
00:05:53,186 --> 00:05:56,022
<i>And if someday, life gets heavy,</i>

75
00:05:57,440 --> 00:05:59,192
<i>or when the road is hard to see,</i>

76
00:06:00,693 --> 00:06:02,904
<i>when your world is full of questions,</i>

77
00:06:03,988 --> 00:06:06,574
<i>you can always run to me.</i>

78
00:06:08,284 --> 00:06:15,291
["ABELYANA" CONTINUES]

79
00:06:36,312 --> 00:06:43,027
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

80
00:07:22,608 --> 00:07:25,778
Auntie Pres, even if you were trespassing,
what she did was still wrong!

81
00:07:25,862 --> 00:07:28,322
We should report her!
You got hurt.

82
00:07:28,406 --> 00:07:29,949
Are you all right?

83
00:07:30,533 --> 00:07:31,951
I'm all right, Billy.

84
00:07:32,034 --> 00:07:33,911
But you have to look at this.

85
00:07:36,289 --> 00:07:41,752
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

86
00:07:41,836 --> 00:07:44,714
[PRECIOUS] We were shocked
when we saw that there.

87
00:07:49,927 --> 00:07:51,971
So they've been keeping
an eye on me for a while now?

88
00:07:54,682 --> 00:07:56,767
Auntie Pres, right from the start,

89
00:07:56,851 --> 00:07:58,895
they've been planning this all along.

90
00:07:58,978 --> 00:08:02,190
That's why we need to be more careful.

91
00:08:02,273 --> 00:08:05,318
[PRECIOUS] We don't know why
they're going after you.

92
00:08:05,401 --> 00:08:07,028
The only thing we can be sure of is that

93
00:08:07,111 --> 00:08:10,406
Mariela and Bea are both dangerous.

94
00:08:10,490 --> 00:08:12,200
And now, we have proof

95
00:08:12,283 --> 00:08:13,826
that they are not in their right minds.

96
00:08:15,578 --> 00:08:17,371
[EXHALES SHARPLY] Billy, I'm sorry.

97
00:08:18,164 --> 00:08:21,667
I just really wanted to help you
lessen your problems,

98
00:08:21,751 --> 00:08:23,836
and find out why they're so mad at you.

99
00:08:23,920 --> 00:08:26,464
But it seems that
I've only made things worse.

100
00:08:26,547 --> 00:08:32,887
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

101
00:08:37,058 --> 00:08:38,351
[CRISELDA] Look at what you've done!

102
00:08:38,434 --> 00:08:41,354
- My God, I was panicking.
- [BEA] Hey! What's happening here?

103
00:08:41,437 --> 00:08:43,147
[CRISELDA]
What if you'd actually killed her?

104
00:08:43,231 --> 00:08:45,358
[BEA] Ma! Wait a minute.
What's happening here?

105
00:08:45,441 --> 00:08:47,527
We should be the ones asking you that.

106
00:08:47,610 --> 00:08:49,529
I'll let you sleep here
in my unit for tonight,

107
00:08:49,612 --> 00:08:51,948
but you should be gone by the morning!

108
00:08:52,031 --> 00:08:55,201
Wait, Ms. Criselda. Don't do this to us.

109
00:08:55,284 --> 00:08:57,286
You haven't paid rent
for two months already!

110
00:08:57,370 --> 00:08:59,288
If I'd only known that you were criminals,

111
00:08:59,372 --> 00:09:00,831
I never would have let you live here!

112
00:09:00,915 --> 00:09:03,167
Wait a second. Please watch
your mouth, Ms. Criselda.

113
00:09:03,251 --> 00:09:04,544
Who are you calling criminals?

114
00:09:04,627 --> 00:09:07,171
Your mother almost murdered someone!

115
00:09:07,255 --> 00:09:09,549
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

116
00:09:09,632 --> 00:09:10,800
[BEA] Ma?

117
00:09:10,883 --> 00:09:11,926
What?

118
00:09:12,969 --> 00:09:15,096
Why are you still standing there, huh?

119
00:09:15,179 --> 00:09:17,348
The show's over, okay?

120
00:09:17,431 --> 00:09:19,559
Stop watching us, you nosy bastards.

121
00:09:20,518 --> 00:09:21,852
Go home!

122
00:09:23,938 --> 00:09:25,314
How crazy.

123
00:09:25,398 --> 00:09:27,316
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

124
00:09:27,400 --> 00:09:28,526
Ma.

125
00:09:28,609 --> 00:09:29,694
[BEA] Ma.

126
00:09:29,777 --> 00:09:31,654
What was Ms. Criselda talking about?

127
00:09:31,737 --> 00:09:33,072
You almost murdered someone?

128
00:09:37,243 --> 00:09:40,246
[PAPER RUSTLING]

129
00:09:40,329 --> 00:09:46,877
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

130
00:09:46,961 --> 00:09:48,296
Um…

131
00:09:53,926 --> 00:09:55,636
That's for next month's rent.

132
00:09:56,220 --> 00:09:57,138
Oh.

133
00:09:57,221 --> 00:09:59,056
Where did you get this?

134
00:09:59,140 --> 00:10:01,517
It's from the last salary you gave me.

135
00:10:01,601 --> 00:10:02,977
What about the month after that?

136
00:10:03,060 --> 00:10:04,353
Where will you get the money then?

137
00:10:04,437 --> 00:10:05,730
I'll just find a way.

138
00:10:05,813 --> 00:10:07,982
I can talk to Ma'am Ronquillo.

139
00:10:08,065 --> 00:10:09,942
So you're not going to leave anymore?

140
00:10:10,693 --> 00:10:13,070
Billy gave me the chance to see Oliver.

141
00:10:13,154 --> 00:10:15,406
[ENRICO] It's also my chance
to make it up to them.

142
00:10:15,489 --> 00:10:18,451
I hope this is the start of my children
letting me into their lives again.

143
00:10:18,534 --> 00:10:20,620
I'm really happy for you, Eric.

144
00:10:21,495 --> 00:10:22,913
Thank you.

145
00:10:22,997 --> 00:10:24,165
[CHUCKLES]

146
00:10:25,416 --> 00:10:27,835
[CRYING] They're living lavishly.

147
00:10:27,918 --> 00:10:30,212
They have a beautiful house.

148
00:10:30,296 --> 00:10:33,299
They're living a luxurious life.

149
00:10:33,966 --> 00:10:38,346
And now, they have your father too!

150
00:10:38,429 --> 00:10:40,431
While us?

151
00:10:40,514 --> 00:10:44,393
[SOBS] We've got nothing left!

152
00:10:45,519 --> 00:10:47,980
Look at what we have, Bea!

153
00:10:49,190 --> 00:10:51,150
Nothing!

154
00:10:51,233 --> 00:10:52,360
Ma…

155
00:10:53,444 --> 00:10:55,071
[SOBS]

156
00:10:55,154 --> 00:10:57,990
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

157
00:10:58,074 --> 00:11:02,912
Now I understand
why you're so furious at that Billy!

158
00:11:03,579 --> 00:11:06,582
But you should've told me
about it right away!

159
00:11:06,666 --> 00:11:08,709
You knew that your father had come back!

160
00:11:08,793 --> 00:11:11,087
Ma, believe me, I wanted to.

161
00:11:11,170 --> 00:11:15,216
But I wanted to tell you about it
once I'd already avenged you.

162
00:11:15,800 --> 00:11:17,968
That devil-spawn father of yours

163
00:11:18,052 --> 00:11:20,262
is together with Billy's aunt!

164
00:11:20,346 --> 00:11:22,306
I'll kill them!

165
00:11:22,390 --> 00:11:23,766
I'll kill them both!

166
00:11:23,849 --> 00:11:25,434
I'll kill them!

167
00:11:25,518 --> 00:11:27,478
- [BEA] Ma! Ma!
- [SOBBING]

168
00:11:28,145 --> 00:11:29,105
Ma!

169
00:11:30,022 --> 00:11:32,733
This is what I was worried about!
This is what I was trying to stop!

170
00:11:32,817 --> 00:11:35,277
That's why I didn't tell you about it!

171
00:11:35,361 --> 00:11:36,737
[MARIELA] Am I in the wrong?

172
00:11:37,363 --> 00:11:39,198
It's only right for them to die!

173
00:11:39,281 --> 00:11:40,449
Ma…

174
00:11:40,533 --> 00:11:41,575
Ma.

175
00:11:42,201 --> 00:11:43,911
No one's dying.

176
00:11:43,994 --> 00:11:46,122
No one's dying, okay?

177
00:11:46,205 --> 00:11:50,167
And most of all,
I don't want you to hurt yourself.

178
00:11:50,251 --> 00:11:52,545
What if you end up
trying to kill yourself again?!

179
00:11:52,628 --> 00:11:54,672
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

180
00:11:54,755 --> 00:11:56,882
I won't do it ever again.

181
00:11:58,259 --> 00:12:00,177
I regret doing it.

182
00:12:00,261 --> 00:12:03,347
It's what caused your sister's
death. [SOBBING]

183
00:12:04,557 --> 00:12:06,016
[SHUSHING]

184
00:12:06,934 --> 00:12:09,520
- [SNIFFLING, SOBBING]
- There, there…

185
00:12:10,896 --> 00:12:12,189
That's why, Ma,

186
00:12:12,273 --> 00:12:15,276
you have to promise me.

187
00:12:15,359 --> 00:12:18,404
Please, Ma, promise me

188
00:12:18,988 --> 00:12:24,535
that you'll leave our revenge to me.

189
00:12:25,119 --> 00:12:26,871
I will avenge us.

190
00:12:26,954 --> 00:12:31,041
I will avenge us both, okay?

191
00:12:31,125 --> 00:12:34,545
Ma, please, okay? Please.

192
00:12:34,628 --> 00:12:36,505
Leave it up to me.

193
00:12:38,466 --> 00:12:39,675
I'll do it.

194
00:12:39,758 --> 00:12:46,307
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

195
00:13:00,404 --> 00:13:01,363
[JORDAN] Dude?

196
00:13:02,114 --> 00:13:03,199
- Hey.
- What's up?

197
00:13:03,866 --> 00:13:07,036
Bea and her mom are gone from their place.

198
00:13:07,119 --> 00:13:09,455
- Huh?
- The police went there.

199
00:13:10,456 --> 00:13:12,082
So what now?

200
00:13:13,125 --> 00:13:14,460
How are we going to find them?

201
00:13:14,543 --> 00:13:17,338
Isn't this better?
For them to just go away?

202
00:13:17,421 --> 00:13:18,964
So they won't bother you anymore.

203
00:13:19,048 --> 00:13:21,008
- Dude, come on.
- I'm just worried about you.

204
00:13:21,091 --> 00:13:23,552
Your safety. Look,
I don't want you to get hurt.

205
00:13:23,636 --> 00:13:25,846
I mean, I can't always be there for you.

206
00:13:25,930 --> 00:13:29,266
Okay, Jordan, thank you.
I know you're just concerned.

207
00:13:29,350 --> 00:13:32,770
If it were just about me,
fine, I'd let it slide.

208
00:13:32,853 --> 00:13:34,230
But we're talking about Auntie Pres.

209
00:13:34,313 --> 00:13:36,232
I won't just let it go. Sorry.

210
00:13:39,735 --> 00:13:46,700
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

211
00:14:02,174 --> 00:14:04,343
[TONI] What a beautiful bouquet!

212
00:14:04,426 --> 00:14:06,011
Who's it from, Val?

213
00:14:07,304 --> 00:14:10,933
Honestly, I don't know.

214
00:14:11,475 --> 00:14:13,435
Wow! Real main character energy, huh?

215
00:14:13,936 --> 00:14:16,730
Wow! You have a new admirer, twinny?

216
00:14:16,814 --> 00:14:20,317
Wait, how come I don't know?
It's not in your vlogs.

217
00:14:20,401 --> 00:14:21,652
Maybe it's from a fan?

218
00:14:22,945 --> 00:14:25,281
Look, there's a letter. Open it.

219
00:14:25,364 --> 00:14:26,991
- Oh, there it is.
- Go.

220
00:14:27,074 --> 00:14:32,997
- [PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]
- [PAPER RUSTLES]

221
00:14:38,419 --> 00:14:40,880
- [PAPER RUSTLES]
- [CHARM] What?

222
00:14:44,341 --> 00:14:45,634
- Oh…
- What's wrong?

223
00:14:45,718 --> 00:14:47,595
- [GROANS]
- What the…?

224
00:14:49,430 --> 00:14:50,639
It's from Robbie.

225
00:14:50,723 --> 00:14:52,266
Sorry, but…

226
00:14:52,766 --> 00:14:53,851
No.

227
00:14:54,852 --> 00:14:56,478
Wait. Robbie who?

228
00:14:58,105 --> 00:15:01,567
Robbie, as in Jade & Jude's Robbie.

229
00:15:03,068 --> 00:15:04,653
Jordan's bartender.

230
00:15:04,737 --> 00:15:05,905
What a waste.

231
00:15:06,655 --> 00:15:09,617
But hopefully, I'll get one next time.

232
00:15:10,242 --> 00:15:12,119
But I prefer periwinkles.

233
00:15:13,454 --> 00:15:16,373
Robbie, my love, choose me instead.

234
00:15:16,457 --> 00:15:20,711
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

235
00:15:20,794 --> 00:15:21,754
[PHONE RINGING]

236
00:15:21,837 --> 00:15:23,339
Billy, we're here.

237
00:15:23,422 --> 00:15:25,215
- Thank you, Billy.
- [BILLY] <i>Oliver.</i>

238
00:15:25,299 --> 00:15:28,218
Remember our deal, okay? Just one hour.

239
00:15:28,302 --> 00:15:30,304
- Can we make it two hours?
- [MOUTH CLICKS]

240
00:15:30,387 --> 00:15:31,722
Don't ask for more.

241
00:15:31,805 --> 00:15:33,557
- You still have homework to do.
- Okay.

242
00:15:33,641 --> 00:15:36,101
<i>You're lucky your sister even let you.</i>
<i>Okay then, Billy, bye now.</i>

243
00:15:36,185 --> 00:15:37,061
- Bye!
- Mm-hmm.

244
00:15:38,479 --> 00:15:41,065
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

245
00:15:41,148 --> 00:15:43,150
Come on, let's go inside.

246
00:15:43,984 --> 00:15:45,819
- Pa!
- Are you excited?

247
00:15:48,113 --> 00:15:50,157
Come on, let's go inside.

248
00:15:57,039 --> 00:15:58,707
Chief?

249
00:15:58,791 --> 00:16:01,877
Chief, the draft of our contract
with Sir Peter is ready.

250
00:16:01,961 --> 00:16:04,088
It's in your email for your review.

251
00:16:04,171 --> 00:16:06,090
But I also printed a hard copy.

252
00:16:06,173 --> 00:16:07,341
Okay. Thank you, Blaire.

253
00:16:07,424 --> 00:16:08,550
Okay.

254
00:16:09,635 --> 00:16:10,719
[CHUCKLES]

255
00:16:11,553 --> 00:16:17,351
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

256
00:16:21,814 --> 00:16:23,357
- [UTENSILS CLINK]
- [OLIVER] Hmm, so good!

257
00:16:23,440 --> 00:16:26,402
Oliver, eat slowly.

258
00:16:26,485 --> 00:16:28,320
It's really good, Auntie.

259
00:16:28,404 --> 00:16:29,488
Thank you, Pa.

260
00:16:29,571 --> 00:16:31,323
Do you like it?

261
00:16:31,407 --> 00:16:34,159
The dishes I made
are mostly vegetable dishes.

262
00:16:34,243 --> 00:16:36,078
That's good for you.

263
00:16:36,161 --> 00:16:37,287
Go ahead, keep eating.

264
00:16:37,871 --> 00:16:39,873
What about you? Aren't you going to eat?

265
00:16:40,708 --> 00:16:42,126
- I'm full.
- It's so good.

266
00:16:43,711 --> 00:16:44,545
Auntie…

267
00:16:45,713 --> 00:16:49,174
Can we invite Papa
to my moving-up ceremony?

268
00:16:49,800 --> 00:16:51,635
I got high honors.

269
00:16:51,719 --> 00:16:55,681
Pa, do you want to be the one
to put the medal on me?

270
00:16:58,350 --> 00:16:59,351
What is it?

271
00:16:59,435 --> 00:17:02,062
Aren't you going to be at
my moving-up ceremony anymore?

272
00:17:02,146 --> 00:17:03,731
Are you leaving?

273
00:17:04,398 --> 00:17:06,358
Are you going to leave us again?

274
00:17:13,323 --> 00:17:14,950
Remember this, son.

275
00:17:15,701 --> 00:17:17,161
That won't happen again.

276
00:17:17,244 --> 00:17:19,204
From now on, I'll always be here for you.

277
00:17:19,788 --> 00:17:20,956
Thank you, Pa.

278
00:17:21,040 --> 00:17:22,207
Thank you.

279
00:17:22,291 --> 00:17:24,668
Ah! I have a surprise for you.

280
00:17:24,752 --> 00:17:25,586
- Wait.
- Really?

281
00:17:25,669 --> 00:17:27,087
- What is it?
- Give me five minutes.

282
00:17:27,171 --> 00:17:29,298
- Am I included too?
- Just continue eating.

283
00:17:29,381 --> 00:17:30,299
- Oliver!
- I'll be quick!

284
00:17:30,382 --> 00:17:31,842
We only have 25 minutes left!

285
00:17:31,925 --> 00:17:34,136
- You and your sister agreed!
- This will be quick!

286
00:17:35,971 --> 00:17:37,347
[SIGHS]

287
00:17:37,431 --> 00:17:40,809
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

288
00:17:40,893 --> 00:17:42,936
Please thank Billy

289
00:17:43,020 --> 00:17:47,441
for giving me the chance
to spend time with Oliver.

290
00:17:48,400 --> 00:17:50,027
I hope one day,

291
00:17:51,236 --> 00:17:52,571
we can patch things up too.

292
00:17:52,654 --> 00:17:58,744
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

293
00:18:01,163 --> 00:18:03,832
Don't get your hopes up too much.

294
00:18:04,458 --> 00:18:06,293
Oliver was only given permission
to see you today.

295
00:18:06,376 --> 00:18:09,838
Don't expect him to be allowed
to meet you all the time.

296
00:18:10,672 --> 00:18:12,132
I understand Billy.

297
00:18:12,883 --> 00:18:14,468
I owe her a huge apology.

298
00:18:15,177 --> 00:18:17,137
Billy's mom was pregnant with Oliver

299
00:18:17,846 --> 00:18:19,223
when I walked out on them.

300
00:18:20,224 --> 00:18:23,018
I ran off with another woman to Canada.

301
00:18:24,186 --> 00:18:27,314
We got mixed up in a scam,
and I ended up in prison for a long time.

302
00:18:29,149 --> 00:18:30,526
When I was in prison,

303
00:18:31,819 --> 00:18:33,112
that's where reality hit me.

304
00:18:34,363 --> 00:18:35,823
That's where I learned my lesson.

305
00:18:37,032 --> 00:18:39,159
I was so stupid,
and I was a complete jerk.

306
00:18:40,119 --> 00:18:42,287
I hurt all the people I love.

307
00:18:42,913 --> 00:18:43,872
And now,

308
00:18:44,706 --> 00:18:47,167
I'm paying for all my mistakes.

309
00:18:52,256 --> 00:18:53,799
You're right, Precious.

310
00:18:54,716 --> 00:18:55,926
I deceived you.

311
00:18:57,094 --> 00:18:58,720
I deceived Oliver.

312
00:18:58,804 --> 00:19:01,223
I pretended to be someone else
to be with him.

313
00:19:01,974 --> 00:19:03,767
But what I felt for you…

314
00:19:03,851 --> 00:19:06,061
I didn't mean for it to happen.

315
00:19:07,146 --> 00:19:09,231
I didn't want to hurt you,

316
00:19:09,314 --> 00:19:11,066
but I couldn't tell you the truth either.

317
00:19:12,025 --> 00:19:14,361
But even though I wasn't honest with you,

318
00:19:14,444 --> 00:19:16,905
the love I have for my children

319
00:19:17,489 --> 00:19:18,574
and for you…

320
00:19:20,659 --> 00:19:21,702
is real.

321
00:19:21,785 --> 00:19:27,708
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

322
00:19:40,929 --> 00:19:43,807
[OLIVER] <i>I hope Billy is</i>
<i>with us next time.</i>

323
00:19:44,850 --> 00:19:46,560
<i>- Bye, Pa!</i>
<i>- Be good, okay?</i>

324
00:19:46,643 --> 00:19:47,686
[OLIVER] <i>Yes!</i>

325
00:19:51,315 --> 00:19:54,776
<i>Just want to let you guys know that</i>
<i>I'm very excited about this partnership.</i>

326
00:19:54,860 --> 00:19:57,654
<i>Thirty million is a serious investment.</i>

327
00:19:57,738 --> 00:19:58,697
<i>Yes, it is.</i>

328
00:19:58,780 --> 00:20:01,533
[BILLY] <i>Thank you so much again for</i>
<i>your trust. We won't take it lightly.</i>

329
00:20:01,617 --> 00:20:02,701
- [PETER] <i>Right.</i>
- [JORDAN]<i> Yes, thank you.</i>

330
00:20:02,784 --> 00:20:04,119
[PETER]
<i>…as LoveList</i>

331
00:20:04,203 --> 00:20:07,998
<i>goes from a regional brand</i>
<i>to a global brand.</i>

332
00:20:09,333 --> 00:20:11,210
[ALL] <i>Cheers!</i>

333
00:20:11,293 --> 00:20:12,461
- [MARJ] <i>Whoo-hoo!</i>
- [RALPH] <i>Yeah!</i>

334
00:20:12,544 --> 00:20:13,754
- [BILLY]<i> Congrats!</i>
- [RALPH]<i> Whoo!</i>

335
00:20:13,837 --> 00:20:15,088
[PETER]<i> What are</i>
<i>you looking at?</i>

336
00:20:16,131 --> 00:20:19,551
<i>I can't believe you're single.</i>

337
00:20:24,765 --> 00:20:25,933
<i>It's so hot.</i>

338
00:20:26,016 --> 00:20:28,602
<i>So, you believe in online dating?</i>

339
00:20:29,228 --> 00:20:31,980
<i>I hope I can find</i>

340
00:20:32,689 --> 00:20:33,774
<i>my match.</i>

341
00:20:37,527 --> 00:20:38,904
<i>Mm-hmm.</i>
